Renders by the deadline only on screens refreshing at most as fast as
NIRI_RENDER_DEADLINE_UP_TO_HZ says, in whole hertz, as niri starts, and
at once on faster ones, even while the deadline is wanted. With nothing
set, every rate defers as renders-by-the-deadline.patch had it; one set
but not whole hertz defers no rate, so a typo can't reach a fast screen,
and niri logs the ceiling it read. On Joel's
own GPU the deadline missed no vblank in 3 hours on a 60 Hz screen and
took a median 6 ms off a launcher drawer's trip to it, but missed 8 in
its first 20 s on the 120 Hz panel, whose refresh leaves too little room
to render late in (18 November). Asked through the environment, as the
deadline itself is, so it adds no setting a niri before it would refuse.
Ours, made on the rest.

